# Local Network Publishing

After completing user-requested application changes:

1. Run the relevant backend and frontend checks.
2. If checks pass, run `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/publish-kronos-lan.ps1 -SkipChecks`.
3. Confirm both the frontend and proxied API health endpoint respond.
4. Include the local-network URL in the final handoff.

Do not publish broken builds. Documentation-only changes do not require republishing.
The backend stays on loopback; LAN clients access it through the frontend proxy.
